<title>SWEDEN: Autoliv posts 5 pct rise in Q1 profit.</title>
<headline>Autoliv posts 5 pct rise in Q1 profit.</headline>
<dateline>STOCKHOLM 1997-04-22</dateline>
<text>
<p>Swedish car seatbelt and airbag maker Autoliv on Tuesday posted its results for the first three months of 1997, ending March 31.</p>
<p>					(million crowns unless stated)</p>
<p> Profit after fin items		    316 vs   300</p>
<p> Sales					 3,255 vs 2,983</p>
<p> Earnings per share (SKR)		 3.78 vs  3.50</p>
<p> Operating costs			   2,952 vs 2,699</p>
<p> Operating profit			    303 vs   284</p>
<p> Associated interests			 15 vs    12</p>
<p> Net fin items			 CHARGE  2 vs     4 CREDIT</p>
<p> Tax					     105 vs   108</p>
<p> Minorities			    CHARGE  3 vs   NIL</p>
<p> Net profit				    208 vs   192</p>
<p>NOTE -- A Reuter poll found market analysts expected Autoliv to post a profit after financial items of 319 million crowns for the first quarter of 1997.</p>
<p>-- Stockholm newsroom +46-8-700 1017</p>
</text>
